_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Do not allow fail-open when `blockUrl` matches blocklist.**

At Line 24-27, returning early means blocked navigations can proceed if `blockUrl` is misconfigured. Fall back to a safe URL (e.g., `about:blank`) instead of returning.


<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 function redirectToBlockUrl(tabId, currentUrl, blockUrl, blockPatterns) {
-  if (currentUrl === blockUrl) return;
-  if (urlMatchesAnyPattern(blockUrl, blockPatterns)) {
+  let targetUrl = blockUrl;
+  if (urlMatchesAnyPattern(targetUrl, blockPatterns)) {
     console.warn('[journal-blocker] blockUrl matches blocklist; refusing to redirect');
-    return;
+    targetUrl = DEFAULT_SETTINGS.blockUrl;
   }
-  chrome.tabs.update(tabId, { url: blockUrl });
+  if (currentUrl === targetUrl) return;
+  chrome.tabs.update(tabId, { url: targetUrl });
 }
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@service-worker.js` around lines 24 - 27, The current early return when
urlMatchesAnyPattern(blockUrl, blockPatterns) lets a blocked navigation
continue; instead, when that check is true, respond with a safe fallback (e.g.,
redirect/navigation to "about:blank" or an explicit safe Response) rather than
returning. Locate the blockUrl check (the urlMatchesAnyPattern(blockUrl,
blockPatterns) branch) and replace the return with logic that sends a blocking
response for navigations—use the service worker's response mechanism (e.g.,
event.respondWith with a safe Response/redirect or client navigation to a
known-safe URL) so blocked URLs never fail open.
```

</details>

